# Do Action sends the command CMB_action names - after "Are you sure", except for five entries.
#
# CMB_action lists FlightData.actions. Battery_Reset takes the generic path: the question, then
# doCommand(BATTERY_RESET, 0xff, 100, 0, ...) - which SITL accepts. Answering No sends nothing.
# System_Time is one of the five handled before the question and goes straight away.
# `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:183-206, 1680-1878`
#
# Needs SITL: tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-doaction.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 7

# The Actions grid is on the Actions page, tabActions; the strip opens on Quick, as
# tabControlactions.SelectedIndex = 0 has it. `GCSViews/FlightData.Designer.cs:595-611`
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click fly-tab-actions
expect fly.tab tabActions

expect fly.action Loiter_Unlim
click fly-action-list
click fly-action-Battery_Reset
expect fly.action Battery_Reset

# No: nothing goes.
click fly-doaction
expect fly.prompt ~ Are you sure you want to do Battery_Reset
click fly-prompt-cancel
expect fly.prompt none
expect fly.sent nothing yet

# Escape is the message box's No, its CancelButton: the question has no box to type in, and
# still hears the key. `ExtLibs/Controls/CustomMessageBox.cs:317`
click fly-doaction
expect fly.prompt ~ Are you sure you want to do Battery_Reset
key Escape
expect fly.prompt none
expect fly.sent nothing yet

# Yes: the command, with the C#'s parameters, and the vehicle's answer.
click fly-doaction
click fly-prompt-ok
expect fly.prompt none
expect fly.sent COMMAND_LONG MAV_CMD_BATTERY_RESET 255,100,0,0,0,0,0
expect fly.ack ~ MAV_CMD_BATTERY_RESET: accepted

# System_Time: no question.
click fly-action-list
click fly-action-System_Time
click fly-doaction
expect fly.prompt none
expect fly.sent ~ SYSTEM_TIME time_unix_usec=
